WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.450
Look at a butterfly, a rock and a chair.

00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:05.475
Which one is a living thing?

00:00:05.475 --> 00:00:07.462
The butterfly is alive.

00:00:07.462 --> 00:00:09.150
The rock and the chair are not.

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:12.662
A living thing grows and changes during its life.

00:00:12.662 --> 00:00:19.962
Moving by itself is not our only clue: a plant is alive even though it cannot walk across the room.

00:00:19.962 --> 00:00:22.000
Science begins with evidence.

00:00:23.167 --> 00:00:26.917
Imagine looking at photographs of a horse at different ages.

00:00:26.917 --> 00:00:28.804
The young horse is smaller.

00:00:28.804 --> 00:00:31.767
As it grows, it becomes an adult horse.

00:00:31.767 --> 00:00:33.817
It does not become a different kind of animal.

00:00:33.817 --> 00:00:36.567
Living things do not stay babies forever.

00:00:36.567 --> 00:00:40.467
Growth and change help us describe the stages of their lives.

00:00:40.467 --> 00:00:43.442
Can you explain what changed and what stayed the same?

00:00:44.625 --> 00:00:49.675
A life cycle describes the stages of growth and change in a living thing.

00:00:49.675 --> 00:00:52.300
It is not a sleeping place or a type of food.

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:55.613
Animals have life cycles, and plants do too.

00:00:55.613 --> 00:01:00.450
An apple tree can grow from a seed into a young plant and then a mature tree.

00:01:00.450 --> 00:01:04.213
That tree can produce seeds, so the cycle can begin again.

00:01:05.417 --> 00:01:10.479
All living things have life cycles, but their stages are not exactly the same.

00:01:10.479 --> 00:01:13.529
A tiger cub grows into an adult tiger.

00:01:13.529 --> 00:01:18.217
A frog in the life cycle shown on your worksheet passes through a tadpole stage.

00:01:18.217 --> 00:01:19.492
A tiger does not.

00:01:19.492 --> 00:01:26.529
When you read a sentence with the word all or exactly, check whether the evidence really supports such a strong claim.

00:01:27.708 --> 00:01:36.858
Here is your science toolkit: identify a living thing, describe how it grows and changes, and connect the stages of its life cycle.

00:01:36.858 --> 00:01:40.083
Remember that a seed can grow into an apple tree.

00:01:40.083 --> 00:01:42.108
Now investigate the questions.

00:01:42.108 --> 00:01:45.458
Choose an answer, then explain the clue that helped you.

00:01:45.458 --> 00:01:50.896
Being a good scientist means understanding your choice, not just remembering a letter.
